<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">François Tombalbaye</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1918–1975</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Ngarta Tombalbaye</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">François Tombalbaye was a southern Chadian teacher and trade unionist who led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chad">Chad</a> to independence on 11 August 1960 and became its first president. He banned opposition parties, and the dominance of southerners in his government fuelled a rebellion in the north and east from 1965. He was killed in a military coup in April 1975.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francois-tombalbaye.jpg" alt="François Tombalbaye" width="320" height="421" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Moshe Pridan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fran%C3%A7ois_Tombalbaye_1959_(3x4_cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
